    "ideaTitle": "A partition is a numbered slice of the table.",
    "ideaP1": "Notification tables can grow very large. Partitioning splits the rows into <strong>nine smaller pieces</strong> that share the same columns. The service chooses a piece by the day, so it can write a day's notifications into one slice and clear old slices without scanning everything.",
    "ideaP2": "The slices are called <strong>p0 to p8</strong>. They are not nine copies of the data: every notification row belongs to exactly one partition. A day's rows live together, which is what makes cleanup a single, predictable operation.",
